// Contexts parsing in the editor (§4.4): above the parsing unit sees exactly the rules of
// its place - as a full parsing (announced below in the text, in other modules and
// outdated - no); editing the design announcement re-examines the context elements after
// it.
// 
//.
// program: editor_context.vish
open_view module
[2] open_view module
// The line above the syntax twice advert: no record yet - the hole remains a hole
pointer 1 @twice 0 14
key 1 2
// expect: kind="n_hole" pieces=["twice { n += 12; }"] note="ожидалось ';'"
// expect-not: kind="n_call"
// Block brackets (Backspace in indentation - translation of the line): the block is disassembled - the same
pointer 1 @n:3 0 0
key 1 Backspace
// expect: kind="n_block"
// expect: kind="n_hole" pieces=["twice { n += 12; }"] note="ожидалось ';'"
// expect-not: kind="n_call"
// announcement when ceased to be a design (exp - type, not mode): the instruction with the
// tail after it - a hole, both clients; record twice - as it was
pointer 1 @expr 0 4
key 1 Backspace
// expect: курсор: when(c, exp‸ body) {
// expect: kind="n_hole" pieces=["when(n > 1) n += 10;"] note="ожидалось ';'"
// expect: kind="n_call" pieces=["twice " #
// expect: другому клиенту:⏎update
// Again design, again tail challenge.
key 1 r
// expect: курсор: when(c, expr‸ body) {
// expect-not: pieces=["when(n > 1) n += 10;"]
// expect: kind="n_ident" pieces=["when"]
